{
  "name": "What to Expect During Your Roof Material Condition Assessment",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1: Getting a roof material condition assessment shouldn't be a mystery",
      "text": "Getting a roof material condition assessment shouldn't be a mystery. We believe in clear communication every step of the way so you know exactly what's happening. When you schedule an assessment with a trusted local company like ours, you're getting more than just someone looking at your roof; you're getting a detailed evaluation designed to protect your home from Texas weather.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 2: First, we'll confirm your roof's basic info, like its system type a…",
      "text": "First, we'll confirm your roof's basic info, like its system type and any installation history you might have. This gives us a baseline before we even get up there.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 2
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 3: Next, our team conducts a thorough visual inspection of all accessi…",
      "text": "Next, our team conducts a thorough visual inspection of all accessible roof areas. We're safely looking at your shingles or other surface materials, the roof edges, and all those important drainage components. We're checking for anything that looks out of place, from surface defects to loose seams and fasteners.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 3
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 4: Then, we'll examine any accessible attic or interior spaces for sig…",
      "text": "Then, we'll examine any accessible attic or interior spaces for signs of trouble, like water stains, damp spots, or even mold indicators. Sometimes, a roof issue shows itself from the inside out.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 4
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 5: We document everything we find with photographs and clear descripti…",
      "text": "We document everything we find with photographs and clear descriptions. This way, you can see exactly what we're talking about, where the issues are, and how severe they might be. We'll also help identify if your roof is built for Texas conditions and if durable metal roofing could be a good long-term option for you.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 5
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 6: Finally, we'll explain our findings in plain language, outlining th…",
      "text": "Finally, we'll explain our findings in plain language, outlining the condition, potential remaining service life, and whether you might need maintenance, repair, or even a full replacement. We'll also cover the limitations of our non-destructive assessment, so you know what we can and can't see without further investigation.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 6
    },
    {
      "name": "Step 7: It's all about making sure you have peace of mind and can make info…",
      "text": "It's all about making sure you have peace of mind and can make informed decisions. We're locally owned and operated, built on referrals, and fully insured. For a transparent roof material condition assessment, reach out to Discounted Roofing Co. at (254) 205-7067.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 7
    }
  ],
  "@type": "HowTo",
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "speakable": {
    "@type": "SpeakableSpecification",
    "cssSelector": [
      "h1",
      ".howto-step",
      "[itemprop=\"step\"]"
    ]
  },
  "totalTime": "PT30M",
